  "answer": "To reduce the risk of credit assignment failure caused by delayed rewards, it has been proposed to integrate RUDDER reward redistribution during reinforcement learning fine-tuning (https://arxiv.org/abs/1806.07857). This mechanism uses an LSTM to predict the episode-wide return at every time step and assigns redistributed rewards based on the differences between consecutive predictions (https://arxiv.org/abs/1806.07857). By shifting delayed rewards backward along the trajectory, the expected future reward for each step becomes near zero, which removes sources of bias and variance and leads to faster, lower-variance learning (https://arxiv.org/abs/1806.07857)."
